    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d584">

                <pb facs="0710" n="704" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg704"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.248/218: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Standley</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kuibyshev</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-05-26T15:00:00+03:00">May 26, 1942—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>447. Department’s 220, May 1 [<hi rendition="#italic">11</hi>], 10 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">9</hi>] p.m. In addition to my own personal approach on
                    the subject to Stalin, Molotov, Mikoyan, Vyshinsky and Lozovsky, I have been at
                    pains to have the matter of air routes taken up on every possible opportunity by
                    the Military and Naval Attachés and by General Faymonville. Michela has sent the
                    War Department today a personal message (his No. 93, May 26<anchor n="92"
                        xml:id="d584-f1"/>) from me to General Marshall<anchor n="93"
                        xml:id="d584-f2"/> outlining the efforts made and the difficulties
                    encountered, and informing him that concrete proposals must be offered if Soviet
                    doubts and suspicions are to be overcome.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Standley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d584-f1" n="92" xml:id="d584-f1-content">
                <p>No copy found in Department files.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d584-f2" n="93" xml:id="d584-f2-content">
                <p>Gen. George C. Marshall, Chief of Staff of the United States Army.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
